worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_handler_rules.js"
  ceiling 804
  rationale "Browser interpreter for data/seed/handler-rules.lino (issue #1085 D1.3). JavaScript-first twin of native handler keys (clarification, punctuation_only_prompt, ill_formed, physical_action_question, opinion_question (the handler-rules interpreter)), added under R997-R999 (2026-10-06); growth is the ported handler, not silent regrowth. Ceiling moved to 694 for issue #1175 R3 (follow-up round, 2026-10-08): the rule interpreter reads the prior_turn condition and the clarification twin passes the dialogue history to it. Ceiling moved to 774 for issue #918 (2026-10-08, R914-6 minimal-core batch): the interpreter gained three domain-free primitives the native rule interpreter gained with it, the role_slot capture, the stable_id value and the evidence condition, plus the handlerRuleSetClaims probe; with them conversation_topic, source_refresh and source_conflict left their bespoke twins in formal_ai_worker_capabilities_and_runtime_rules.js, formal_ai_worker_native_lanes.js and formal_ai_worker_code_plans.js (and their Rust functions) for seed rules, so the growth is generic machinery replacing three handlers, not regrowth. Ceiling moved to 802 the same day for the fourth issue #918 batch: the interpreter gained the quoted and network_snapshot values and intent templating, with which the network_query snapshot, concept introspection and user filter became seed rules in both runtimes; the browser twin gained the two branches it used to leave native. Ceiling moved to 817 the same day for the sixth issue #918 batch: handlerRulesPolicy reads the policy blocks of the rule document, the browser half of rule_interpreter::handler_policy. Ceiling moved 817 to 828 for issue #1175 R3 (last five rows, 2026-10-08): the `operand` value source captures the operand a claim-evidence reader extracts (CLAIM_OPERANDS), as rust ValueSource::Operand does, so a rule answers about the same operand its claim row admits on (R999: the twin grows with the reader it mirrors). Ceiling 833 (2026-10-08, PR #1188, R1013 server parity): the `cue_set` condition reads `cue_lexicon::matches` (rust/src/cue_lexicon.rs, token / substring / prefix modes) over the cue sets a caller carries in the rule context, so the server's intent record promotes `concept_lookup` from data/seed/handler-promotions.lino as rust/src/handler_promotion.rs `promoted_relevants` does; the browser rule sets carry no cue sets and keep their dedicated handlers. Ceiling moved to 899 for the issue #918 algorithm batch (2026-10-08): the interpreter gains the operation condition (the seeded operation vocabulary, operationMatchesSlug), the table value (a row of a table block by containment or by key, with its cached reader of the table blocks) and the response value (a seeded response under a templated intent), the domain-free primitives the native interpreter gained in rust/src/rule_interpreter/values.rs; they replace the 58 lines of the deleted algorithm handler of formal_ai_worker_code_plans.js. Ceiling moved to 913 for the issue #918 document batch (2026-10-08): the exact-key table lookup and the exported handlerRulesTableRow reader, the twin of rule_interpreter::handler_table_row, let native-primitive handlers read their cue tables from data/seed/handler-rules.lino; they replace 65 lines of inline document cue lists and templates in formal_ai_worker_code_plans.js (260 -> 195), a net drop of 51. Ceiling moved to 951 for the issue #918 calendar batch (2026-10-08): handlerRulesTableValue and handlerRulesTableKeys, the twins of rule_interpreter::handler_table_value and handler_table_rows, and handlerRulesFillOnce, the twin of seed::fill_template_once, let the calendar handlers read their weekday names, default title and cue lists from the calendar_* tables and fill their seeded sentences in one pass; they replace the inline name tables, cue arrays and templates of formal_ai_worker_calendar_and_proofs.js (1319 -> 1206) and formal_ai_worker_calendar_offset.js (570 -> 532), a net drop of 113. Ceiling lowered 951 to 804 for R1188-U20 (2026-10-08): the subjects and captured value sources moved, unchanged, to formal_ai_worker_handler_rule_values.js, the twin of rust/src/rule_interpreter/values.rs."
